<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan gold rates seen falling on strong rupee.</title>
<headline>Pakistan gold rates seen falling on strong rupee.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan gold rates are likely to fall in the next few days as the rupee strengthens against the dollar in the kerb market, dealers said on Monday.</p>
<p>The strong rupee, which closed at 40.90 to the dollar on Sunday, up from 41.30 on Tuesday, depressed gold prices last week, but silver prices were unchanged, one dealer said.</p>
<p>    24 carat gold in rupees per 10 grammes Feb 16   Feb 11</p>
<p>							 4,637    4,718</p>
<p>    Silver per 1,000 grammes		   7,715    7,715</p>
<p>($1 = 40.22 rupees)</p>
